    "result_text": "The only remaining references are in the acceptance test itself, where they are intentional (asserting the old fields are gone). The implementation is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI unified `customerCode` and `membershipNumber` into a single `memberId` and removed the standalone `checkDigit`, formatted `<REGION><FY><HASH8><CHK>`.\n\n**`model/Owner.java`**\n- Renamed the `customerCode`/`customer_code` field+column to `memberId`/`member_id`; replaced its getter/setter.\n- Removed `getMembershipNumber()` and `getCheckDigit()`; converted the Luhn logic into a private `luhnCheckDigit(String)` helper.\n- Replaced `buildCustomerCode()` with `buildMemberId()`: `REGION` + 2-digit fiscal year + the same 8-upper-hex SHA-256(telephone+lastName) HASH8 + a Luhn CHK over the digits of `<REGION><FY><HASH8>`.\n- `getLocality()` now derives the region from `memberId`'s leading letters (via a new `leadingRegion` helper), falling back to the postcode/city derivation before assignment \u2014 so the owner segment (which reads locality) references the memberId.\n- `getFiscalYear()` now reads the FY segment out of `memberId`, falling back to the registration date when the id isn't set yet.\n\n**`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`**\n- Create path uses `setMemberId(deduplicateMemberId(buildMemberId()))`; collision handling (`deduplicateMemberId`) now applies to the memberId.\n- Audit record: human-readable line and the structured `OWNER_CREATED` event now carry `memberId` instead of `customerCode`/`membershipNumber`.\n\n**`openapi.yml`** \u2014 replaced the `customerCode`/`checkDigit`/`membershipNumber` schema properties with a single `memberId`, and updated the `locality` description.\n\n**DB schemas** (h2/hsqldb/mysql/postgres) \u2014 renamed the `customer_code` column to `member_id` and widened it to hold the longer id (including any dedup suffix).\n\nTest suite: `BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test passed (region prefix, HASH8 presence, and old fields removed all verified).",
