    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe refactor is structurally clean, additive, and idiomatic for this codebase:\n\n- **Helper extraction is well-placed.** `getCheckDigit()` (an instance getter over `customerCode`) became a pure, reusable `private static int luhnCheckDigit(String value)` \u2014 exactly right now that the Luhn digit is a *segment* computed during `buildMemberId()` rather than a standalone exposed field. Similarly, `leadingRegion(String)` is extracted once and shared by both `getLocality()` and `getFiscalYear()`, preserving the \"single source of truth\" intent the original code documented.\n\n- **Dead indirection correctly removed.** The `primaryIdentifier(Owner)` seam in the controller existed solely as \"the sole place to switch when customerCode is unified into the member id.\" That unification has now happened, so inlining `owner.getMemberId()` into both the audit line and `emitOwnerCreatedEvent` is the appropriate collapse rather than leaving a now-pointless wrapper.\n\n- **Logic stays in the right unit.** Member-id *assembly* lives in `Owner.buildMemberId()`; *de-duplication* stays in the controller's renamed `deduplicateMemberId`; the event record and audit log simply carry the new field. No concern leaked into the wrong layer, and the `Owner` model isn't accruing responsibilities it didn't already own.\n\n- **Consistent fallback pattern.** `getFiscalYear()` reading the FY segment out of `memberId` first and falling back to `registrationDate` mirrors the existing `getLocality()` shape (parse-from-identity, else derive), so a maintainer would find it natural.\n\n- **Supporting artifacts tracked coherently.** Schema column rename/width bump across all four dialects, the OpenAPI schema (removing `checkDigit`/`membershipNumber`, reshaping `memberId`/`locality` docs), and the Javadoc all moved in lockstep with no orphaned references to the removed fields.\n\nNo duplication introduced and nothing is becoming a catch-all.",
